 "fields": {
  "description": "theuth is a Cargo workspace of 49 crates (`crates/*`, 1,258 of 1,278 tracked files) plus a TypeScript desktop UI inside `crates/desktop/ui/src` (763 files, 106 k lines). Every crate is a plugin started by the `t` binary (`crates/theuth/src/main.rs`) on a shared `runtime::Runtime` with kameo actors; `crates/rpc` exposes them to the clients over one jsonrpsee WebSocket. This perspective groups the 49 crates into 11 layers chosen by what they depend on and who calls them; the Cargo path-dependency graph (334 edges) is the ground truth behind every arrow. Not shown: every layer depends on `foundation` (runtime/tools/platform are imported by 37, 31 and 24 crates) and `theuth-bin` imports 40 crates to assemble them — those fan-outs are omitted so the picture stays readable. Also outside the picture: `docs/` (542 files, design docs), `packages/` (OpenUI apps), `scripts/`, `site/`, `vendor/` (605 k lines, vendored dependencies), `deploy/`.",
  "context": null,
  "constraint": null,
  "concern": "The dependency graph is star-shaped, not layered: `rpc` imports 37 crates and `agent` is imported by 21 (including `artifact`, `browser`, `meeting`, `talk`, `sandbox`), so \"agent\" is both the core and a shared library. Two files carry a disproportionate share of behaviour: `crates/rpc/src/api.rs` (8,029 lines) and `crates/agent/src/loop_.rs` (10,160 lines). A map that treats crates as units cannot show that; see the request-lifecycle perspective for the file-level path.",
  "todo": null,
  "note": null
 },
